## 💻 Class Implementation (Assignment 10)

The system was implemented in **Java** due to its strong support for object-oriented programming and design patterns.

### Design Decisions

- Classes were directly derived from the UML Class Diagram (Assignment 9)
- Relationships were implemented using object references (composition/association)
- Lists were used to model one-to-many relationships (e.g., Patient → Appointments)
- Encapsulation applied using private attributes with controlled access
- Methods reflect real system actions (e.g., book appointment, assign bed)

### Structure

/src/model contains:
- Patient
- Doctor
- Appointment
- MedicalRecord
- Bed
- MedicationSchedule
- Notification
